IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- Part I, Contributions: Preliminary, ss 1 to 4C (src lines 4-232). Part agent ssc1, LAYER 1.
--
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from legislation.gov.uk
-- (point in time 2026-07-08). It is not the official text and nothing here is
-- "verified against the official text".
--
-- Reading a result (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer):
--   JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE   the text answers, in its own words;
--   NOTHING                  not covered: the text is silent, lists without closing,
--                            includes, leaves a term undefined, points outside these
--                            sources, or limits a grant in its own wording.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every top-level name begins with the label of the provision it implements.
-- Money is a NUMBER in pounds sterling. A "where ..." condition is read like "when":
-- a case outside it is NOTHING (NOTES.md, Marginal readings, M1).
-- There is no regulative rule in this Part: nothing in ss 1-4C names a deadline, an actor
-- who MUST act, or a consequence of not acting (NOTES.md, finding 1).

§ `Part I -- Preliminary, ss 1 to 4C`

§§ `s 1 Outline of contributory system`

-- s 1(1): what the contributions are for. The paragraphs name the two purposes.
DECLARE `s 1(1) Purpose of funds` IS ONE OF
    `s 1(1)(a) paying benefits payable out of the National Insurance Fund and not out of other public money`
    `s 1(1)(b) payments under section 162 of the Administration Act towards the cost of the National Health Service`
    `s 1(1) a purpose the text does not name`

-- src:5 | (1) The funds required—
-- src:6 | (a) for paying such benefits under this Act or any other Act as are payable out of the National Insurance Fund and not out of other public money; and
-- src:7 | (b) for the making of payments under section 162 of the Administration Act towards the cost of the National Health Service,
-- src:8 | shall be provided by means of contributions payable to the Inland Revenue by earners, employers and others, together with the additions under subsection (5) below and amounts payable under section 2 of the Social Security Act 1993.
@ref s 1(1), s 1(1)(a), s 1(1)(b) (src:5-8)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 1(1) Purpose of funds`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1(1) the funds are to be provided by means of contributions payable to the Inland Revenue` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `s 1(1)(a) paying benefits payable out of the National Insurance Fund and not out of other public money` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1(1)(b) payments under section 162 of the Administration Act towards the cost of the National Health Service` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1(1) a purpose the text does not name` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): only the two purposes in (a) and (b) are named

-- s 1(2): the eight classes (the core's `Class of contribution`) and the Act's own description of each.
-- A table of strings copied from the text; the lines of the text are quoted beside each row.
DECLARE `s 1(2) Description of a class` HAS
    `s 1(2) the sections it is payable under` IS A STRING
    `s 1(2) who pays it`                      IS A STRING
    `s 1(2) what it is`                       IS A STRING

-- src:9 | (2) Contributions under this Part of this Act shall be of the following ... classes—
-- src:10 | (a) Class 1, earnings-related, payable under section 6 below, being—
-- src:11 | (i) primary Class 1 contributions from employed earners; and
-- src:12 | (ii) secondary Class 1 contributions from employers and other persons paying earnings;
-- src:13 | (b) Class 1A, payable under section 10 below ... by persons liable to pay secondary Class 1 contributions and certain other persons;
-- src:14 | (bb) Class 1B, payable under section 10A below by persons who are accountable to the Inland Revenue in respect of income tax on general earnings in accordance with a PAYE settlement agreement;
-- src:15 | (c) Class 2, flat-rate, payable ... under section 11 below by self-employed earners;
-- src:16 | (d) Class 3, payable under section 13 or 13A below by earners and others voluntarily with a view to providing entitlement to benefit, or making up entitlement;
-- src:17 | (da) Class 3A, payable by eligible people voluntarily under section 14A with a view to obtaining units of additional pension; and
-- src:18 | (e) Class 4, payable under section 15 below in respect of the profits or gains of a trade, profession or vocation, or under section 18 below in respect of equivalent earnings.
@ref s 1(2) (src:9-18)
GIVEN class IS A `Class of contribution`
GIVETH A `s 1(2) Description of a class`
`s 1(2) the description of the class` MEANS
    CONSIDER class
    -- (a)(i) and (ii): Class 1, earnings-related, payable under section 6
    WHEN `Class 1 primary`   THEN `s 1(2) Description of a class` OF "section 6", "employed earners", "Class 1, earnings-related, primary Class 1 contributions from employed earners"
    WHEN `Class 1 secondary` THEN `s 1(2) Description of a class` OF "section 6", "employers and other persons paying earnings", "Class 1, earnings-related, secondary Class 1 contributions from employers and other persons paying earnings"
    -- (b) Class 1A, payable under section 10
    WHEN `Class 1A`          THEN `s 1(2) Description of a class` OF "section 10", "persons liable to pay secondary Class 1 contributions and certain other persons", "Class 1A"
    -- (bb) Class 1B, payable under section 10A
    WHEN `Class 1B`          THEN `s 1(2) Description of a class` OF "section 10A", "persons who are accountable to the Inland Revenue in respect of income tax on general earnings in accordance with a PAYE settlement agreement", "Class 1B"
    -- (c) Class 2, flat-rate, payable under section 11
    WHEN `Class 2`           THEN `s 1(2) Description of a class` OF "section 11", "self-employed earners", "Class 2, flat-rate"
    -- (d) Class 3, payable under section 13 or 13A
    WHEN `Class 3`           THEN `s 1(2) Description of a class` OF "section 13 or 13A", "earners and others voluntarily", "Class 3, with a view to providing entitlement to benefit, or making up entitlement"
    -- (da) Class 3A, payable under section 14A
    WHEN `Class 3A`          THEN `s 1(2) Description of a class` OF "section 14A", "eligible people voluntarily", "Class 3A, with a view to obtaining units of additional pension"
    -- (e) Class 4, payable under section 15 or section 18
    WHEN `Class 4`           THEN `s 1(2) Description of a class` OF "section 15 or section 18", "persons with profits or gains of a trade, profession or vocation, or equivalent earnings", "Class 4, in respect of the profits or gains of a trade, profession or vocation, or in respect of equivalent earnings"

-- src:23 | (4) Schedule 1 to this Act—
-- src:24 | (a) shall have effect with respect to the computation, collection and recovery of contributions of Classes 1, 1A, 1B, , 3 and 3A, and otherwise with respect to contributions of those classes; and
-- src:25 | (b) shall also, to the extent provided by regulations made under section 18 below, have effect with respect to the computation, collection and recovery of Class 4 contributions, and otherwise with respect to such contributions, ....
@ref s 1(4) (src:23-25)
GIVEN class IS A `Class of contribution`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1(4) Schedule 1 has effect with respect to the computation, collection and recovery of the class` MEANS
    CONSIDER class
    WHEN `Class 1 primary`   THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Class 1 secondary` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Class 1A`          THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Class 1B`          THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Class 2`           THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the list in (a) reads "Classes 1, 1A, 1B, , 3 and 3A", a gap where Class 2 was; the text neither includes nor excludes Class 2
    WHEN `Class 3`           THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Class 3A`          THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Class 4`           THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): (b) gives Schedule 1 effect for Class 4 only "to the extent provided by regulations made under section 18"

-- s 1(5): the Parliamentary addition equals the aggregate of the statutory payments recovered, "as estimated
-- by the Government Actuary or the Deputy Government Actuary". The estimates are inputs.
DECLARE `s 1(5) Statutory payments recovered in a financial year` HAS
    `s 1(5) statutory sick pay`                 IS A NUMBER
    `s 1(5) statutory maternity pay`            IS A NUMBER
    `s 1(5) statutory paternity pay`            IS A NUMBER
    `s 1(5) statutory adoption pay`             IS A NUMBER
    `s 1(5) statutory shared parental pay`      IS A NUMBER
    `s 1(5) statutory parental bereavement pay` IS A NUMBER
    `s 1(5) statutory neonatal care pay`        IS A NUMBER

-- src:26 | (5) For each financial year there shall, by way of addition to contributions, be paid out of money provided by Parliament, in such manner and at such times as the Treasury may determine, amounts the total of which for any such year is equal to the aggregate of all statutory sick pay , statutory maternity pay, statutory paternity pay, statutory adoption pay , statutory shared parental pay , statutory parental bereavement pay and statutory neonatal care pay recovered by employers and others in that year, as estimated by the Government Actuary or the Deputy Government Actuary.
@ref s 1(5) (src:26-26)
GIVEN recovered IS A `s 1(5) Statutory payments recovered in a financial year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 1(5) the total of the amounts to be paid out of money provided by Parliament for the year` MEANS
    recovered's `s 1(5) statutory sick pay`
    PLUS recovered's `s 1(5) statutory maternity pay`
    PLUS recovered's `s 1(5) statutory paternity pay`
    PLUS recovered's `s 1(5) statutory adoption pay`
    PLUS recovered's `s 1(5) statutory shared parental pay`
    PLUS recovered's `s 1(5) statutory parental bereavement pay`
    PLUS recovered's `s 1(5) statutory neonatal care pay`

-- s 1(6): four bars. Each is a flat "No person shall ... unless": a person who does not fulfil the condition
-- is barred (the text says no); a person who does is NOT thereby liable or entitled, the bar is simply
-- not engaged (NOTHING: it is a necessary condition only). "prescribed conditions as to residence or
-- presence in Great Britain" are made by regulations outside these sources: an input.
-- src:27 | (6) No person shall—
-- src:28 | (a) be liable to pay Class 1, Class 1A , Class 1B or Class 2 contributions unless he fulfils prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain;
@ref s 1(6)(a) (src:27-28)
GIVEN class IS A `Class of contribution`
      `the person fulfils the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1(6)(a) the person is liable to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` MEANS
    CONSIDER class
    WHEN `Class 3`  THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (a) names Classes 1, 1A, 1B and 2 only
    WHEN `Class 3A` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (a) names Classes 1, 1A, 1B and 2 only
    WHEN `Class 4`  THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (a) names Classes 1, 1A, 1B and 2 only
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the person fulfils the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain`
        THEN NOTHING                -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless" states a necessary condition; fulfilling it does not make the person liable
        ELSE JUST FALSE             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be liable to pay Class 1, Class 1A , Class 1B or Class 2 contributions unless he fulfils prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain"

-- src:29 | (aa) be treated under section 11(5B) as having actually paid Class 2 contributions unless he fulfils such conditions;
@ref s 1(6)(aa) (src:29-29)
GIVEN `the person fulfils the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1(6)(aa) the person is treated under section 11(5B) as having actually paid Class 2 contributions` MEANS
    IF `the person fulfils the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain`
    THEN NOTHING                    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless" states a necessary condition only
    ELSE JUST FALSE                 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall ... be treated under section 11(5B) as having actually paid Class 2 contributions unless he fulfils such conditions"

-- src:30 | (b) be entitled to pay Class 3 contributions unless he fulfils such conditions; or
@ref s 1(6)(b) (src:30-30)
GIVEN `the person fulfils the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1(6)(b) the person is entitled to pay Class 3 contributions` MEANS
    IF `the person fulfils the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain`
    THEN NOTHING                    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless" states a necessary condition only; sections 13 and 13A say who may pay
    ELSE JUST FALSE                 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall ... be entitled to pay Class 3 contributions unless he fulfils such conditions"

-- src:31 | (c) be entitled to pay Class 1, Class 1A , Class 1B or Class 2 contributions other than those which he is liable to pay, except so far as he is permitted by regulations to pay them.
@ref s 1(6)(c) (src:31-31)
GIVEN class IS A `Class of contribution`
      `the contribution is one the person is liable to pay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is permitted by regulations to pay it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1(6)(c) the person is entitled to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` MEANS
    CONSIDER class
    WHEN `Class 3`  THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (c) names Classes 1, 1A, 1B and 2 only
    WHEN `Class 3A` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (c) names Classes 1, 1A, 1B and 2 only
    WHEN `Class 4`  THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (c) names Classes 1, 1A, 1B and 2 only
    OTHERWISE
        BRANCH
            IF `the contribution is one the person is liable to pay` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): (c) bars only contributions "other than those which he is liable to pay"
            IF `the person is permitted by regulations to pay it` THEN NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "except so far as he is permitted by regulations"
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE                                                      -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall ... be entitled to pay Class 1, Class 1A , Class 1B or Class 2 contributions other than those which he is liable to pay, except so far as he is permitted by regulations to pay them"

§§ `s 2 Categories of earners`

-- s 2(1)(a): "means", so the definition closes: a person who is not gainfully employed in Great Britain under a
-- contract of service or in an office with earnings is not an employed earner. The words "with ... earnings"
-- are shown with an omission in the converter text (src:35): the input records whether the office has earnings (fork F1: the other reading
-- takes the omitted words to lift the qualifier, so that an unpaid elective office would count; NOTES.md, Fork register).
-- src:34 | (1) In this Part of this Act and Parts II to V below—
-- src:35 | (a) “employed earner” means a person who is gainfully employed in Great Britain either under a contract of service, or in an office (including elective office) with ... earnings; and
@ref s 2(1)(a) (src:34-35)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
      `the person is gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the office carries earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1)(a) the person is an employed earner` MEANS
    IF     `the person is gainfully employed`
       AND employment's `carried on in Great Britain`
       AND (   employment's `held under a contract of service`
            OR (employment's `held in an office` AND `the office carries earnings`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employed earner” means a person who is gainfully employed in Great Britain either under a contract of service, or in an office (including elective office) with ... earnings"

-- s 2(1)(b): "self-employed earner" means gainfully employed in Great Britain otherwise than in employed earner's
-- employment. The other employment, if any, does not matter ("whether or not he is also employed in such employment").
-- src:36 | (b) “self-employed earner” means a person who is gainfully employed in Great Britain otherwise than in employed earner’s employment (whether or not he is also employed in such employment).
@ref s 2(1)(b) (src:36-36)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
      `the person is gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the office carries earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1)(b) the person is a self-employed earner` MEANS
    IF     `the person is gainfully employed`
       AND employment's `carried on in Great Britain`
       AND NOT (   employment's `held under a contract of service`
                OR (employment's `held in an office` AND `the office carries earnings`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“self-employed earner” means a person who is gainfully employed in Great Britain otherwise than in employed earner’s employment"

-- s 2(2ZB): "arrangements" include ... : the list is not closed.
DECLARE `s 2(2ZB) Kind of thing` IS ONE OF
    `s 2(2ZB) a scheme`
    `s 2(2ZB) a transaction or series of transactions`
    `s 2(2ZB) an agreement or understanding`
    `s 2(2ZB) associated operations`
    `s 2(2ZB) something else`

-- src:43 | (2ZB) In subsection (2ZA) “arrangements” include any scheme, transaction or series of transactions, agreement or understanding, whether or not legally enforceable, and any associated operations.
@ref s 2(2ZB) (src:43-43)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 2(2ZB) Kind of thing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(2ZB) the thing is an arrangement` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `s 2(2ZB) a scheme`                                      THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2(2ZB) a transaction or series of transactions`       THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2(2ZB) an agreement or understanding`                 THEN JUST TRUE    -- "whether or not legally enforceable": enforceability makes no difference
    WHEN `s 2(2ZB) associated operations`                         THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2(2ZB) something else`                                THEN NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "arrangements” include any scheme ..." does not close the list

-- s 2(3): a person treated as an employed earner by reference to an employment is so treated for all purposes.
-- src:45 | (3) Where a person is to be treated by reference to any employment of his as an employed earner, then he is to be so treated for all purposes of this Act; and references throughout this Act to employed earner’s employment shall be construed accordingly.
@ref s 2(3) (src:45-45)
GIVEN `the person is to be treated by reference to an employment of his as an employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(3) the person is treated as an employed earner for all purposes of this Act` MEANS
    IF `the person is to be treated by reference to an employment of his as an employed earner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a person is to be treated ..." grants for that case only

-- s 2(4): subsections (1) to (3) are subject to s 95 (industrial injuries benefit: employments treated as employed
-- earner's employments). SEAM (not in PLAN.md, new): the answer of section 95 (ssc4) is an input.
-- src:46 | (4) Subsections (1) to (3) above are subject to the provision made by section 95 below as to the employments which are to be treated, for the purposes of industrial injuries benefit, as employed earner’s employments.
@ref s 2(4) (src:46-46)
GIVEN `s 2(1) to (3) say the employment is employed earner's employment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 95 the employment is treated as employed earner's employment for the purposes of industrial injuries benefit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(4) the employment is employed earner's employment for the purposes of industrial injuries benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 95 the employment is treated as employed earner's employment for the purposes of industrial injuries benefit`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE    -- section 95 treats it as one
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `s 2(1) to (3) say the employment is employed earner's employment`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `s 2(1) to (3) say the employment is employed earner's employment`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to the provision made by section 95", whose answer is not supplied
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): neither answer is supplied

-- s 2(5): treated as a self-employed earner as respects any week during any part of which he is such an earner.
-- src:47 | (5) For the purposes of this Act, a person shall be treated as a self-employed earner as respects any week during any part of which he is such an earner (without prejudice to his being also treated as an employed earner as respects that week by reference to any other employment of his).
@ref s 2(5) (src:47-47)
GIVEN `the person is a self-employed earner during some part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(5) the person is treated as a self-employed earner as respects the week` MEANS
    IF `the person is a self-employed earner during some part of the week`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as respects any week during any part of which he is such an earner"

§§ `s 3 "Earnings" and "earner"`

-- s 3(1)(a): "earnings" includes any remuneration or profit derived from an employment: the list is not closed.
-- src:49 | (1) In this Part of this Act and Parts II to V below—
-- src:50 | (a) “earnings” includes any remuneration or profit derived from an employment; and
@ref s 3(1)(a) (src:49-50)
GIVEN `the payment is remuneration or profit derived from an employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(a) the payment is earnings` MEANS
    IF `the payment is remuneration or profit derived from an employment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“earnings” includes any remuneration or profit derived from an employment" does not close the meaning

-- s 3(1)(b): "earner" shall be construed accordingly.
-- src:49 | (1) In this Part of this Act and Parts II to V below—
-- src:50 | (a) “earnings” includes any remuneration or profit derived from an employment; and
-- src:51 | (b) “earner” shall be construed accordingly.
@ref s 3(1)(b) (src:49-51)
GIVEN `the person has remuneration or profit derived from an employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(b) the person is an earner` MEANS
    IF `the person has remuneration or profit derived from an employment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "shall be construed accordingly" says no more than that the meaning follows "earnings"

§§ `s 4 Payments treated as remuneration and earnings`

-- s 4(1)(a): a sum paid in satisfaction (in whole or in part) of an entitlement to one of the listed statutory payments
-- is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment. The core's `Statutory payment` holds all
-- seven kinds the paragraph lists ((iv) is shown blank in this text, src:68).
-- src:63 | (1) For the purposes of section 3 above there shall be treated as remuneration derived from employed earner’s employment—
-- src:64 | (a) any sum paid to or for the benefit of a person in satisfaction (whether in whole or in part) of any entitlement of that person to—
-- src:65 | (i) statutory sick pay; or
-- src:66 | (ii) statutory maternity pay;
-- src:67 | (iii) ... statutory paternity pay;
-- src:68 | (iv) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:69 | (v) statutory adoption pay; ...
-- src:70 | (vi) statutory shared parental pay; ...
-- src:71 | (vii) statutory parental bereavement pay; or
-- src:72 | (viii) statutory neonatal care pay; and
@ref s 4(1)(a) (src:63-72)
GIVEN payment IS A `Statutory payment`
      `the sum is paid to or for the benefit of a person in satisfaction, in whole or in part, of an entitlement to the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1)(a) the sum is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` MEANS
    IF `the sum is paid to or for the benefit of a person in satisfaction, in whole or in part, of an entitlement to the payment`
    THEN
        CONSIDER payment
        WHEN `statutory sick pay`                 THEN JUST TRUE    -- (i)
        WHEN `statutory maternity pay`            THEN JUST TRUE    -- (ii)
        WHEN `statutory paternity pay`            THEN JUST TRUE    -- (iii)
        WHEN `statutory adoption pay`             THEN JUST TRUE    -- (v)
        WHEN `statutory shared parental pay`      THEN JUST TRUE    -- (vi)
        WHEN `statutory parental bereavement pay` THEN JUST TRUE    -- (vii)
        WHEN `statutory neonatal care pay`        THEN JUST TRUE    -- (viii)
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the treatment is of "any sum paid ... in satisfaction ... of any entitlement"

-- s 4(1)(b): a sickness payment made (i) to or for the benefit of the employed earner and (ii) under arrangements
-- to which the secondary contributor has contributed or remains liable to contribute.
-- src:73 | (b) any sickness payment made—
-- src:74 | (i) to or for the benefit of the employed earner; and
-- src:75 | (ii) in accordance with arrangements under which the person who is the secondary contributor in relation to the employment concerned has made, or remains liable to make, payments towards the provision of that sickness payment.
@ref s 4(1)(b) (src:73-75)
GIVEN `the sickness payment is made to or for the benefit of the employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is made in accordance with arrangements under which the secondary contributor has made, or remains liable to make, payments towards its provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1)(b) the sickness payment is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` MEANS
    IF     `the sickness payment is made to or for the benefit of the employed earner`
       AND `the payment is made in accordance with arrangements under which the secondary contributor has made, or remains liable to make, payments towards its provision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) treats "any sickness payment made (i) ... and (ii) ..."; a payment outside both limbs is not addressed

-- s 4(3): "sickness payment" means any payment made in respect of absence from work due to incapacity for work.
-- The text ends the definition with ", ....": the dots mark words not shown (src:77).
-- src:77 | (3) For the purposes of subsections (1) and (2) above “sickness payment” means any payment made in respect of absence from work due to incapacity for work, ....
@ref s 4(3) (src:77-77)
GIVEN `the payment is made in respect of absence from work due to incapacity for work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(3) the payment is a sickness payment` MEANS
    IF `the payment is made in respect of absence from work due to incapacity for work`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“sickness payment” means any payment made in respect of absence from work due to incapacity for work"

-- s 4(4)(a): the gain under s 479 of ITEPA 2003, reduced by the amounts deducted under s 480(1) to (6).
-- The text does not say what follows when the deductions exceed the gain (fork F2): not covered.
-- src:78 | (4) For the purposes of section 3 above there shall be treated as remuneration derived from an employed earner’s employment—
-- src:79 | (a) the amount of any gain calculated under section 479 of ITEPA 2003 in respect of which an amount counts as employment income of the earner under section 476 of that Act (charge on acquisition of securities pursuant to option etc), reduced by any amounts deducted under section 480(1) to (6) of that Act in arriving at the amount counting as such employment income;
@ref s 4(4)(a) (src:78-79)
GIVEN `the gain calculated under section 479 of ITEPA 2003 counts as employment income of the earner under section 476` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gain` IS A NUMBER
      `the amounts deducted under section 480(1) to (6) of that Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 4(4)(a) the amount treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the gain calculated under section 479 of ITEPA 2003 counts as employment income of the earner under section 476` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the treatment is of "the amount of any gain ... in respect of which an amount counts as employment income of the earner under section 476"
        IF `the amounts deducted under section 480(1) to (6) of that Act` GREATER THAN `the gain` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): fork F2, the text does not say what a negative remainder is
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the gain` MINUS `the amounts deducted under section 480(1) to (6) of that Act`)

-- src:78 | (4) For the purposes of section 3 above there shall be treated as remuneration derived from an employed earner’s employment—
-- src:79 | (a) the amount of any gain calculated under section 479 of ITEPA 2003 in respect of which an amount counts as employment income of the earner under section 476 of that Act (charge on acquisition of securities pursuant to option etc), reduced by any amounts deducted under section 480(1) to (6) of that Act in arriving at the amount counting as such employment income;
-- src:80 | (b) any sum paid (or treated as paid) to or for the benefit of the earner which is chargeable to tax by virtue of section 225 or 226 of ITEPA 2003 (taxation of consideration for certain restrictive undertakings).
@ref s 4(4)(b) (src:78-80)
GIVEN `the sum is paid, or treated as paid, to or for the benefit of the earner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum is chargeable to tax by virtue of section 225 or 226 of ITEPA 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(4)(b) the sum is treated as remuneration derived from an employed earner's employment` MEANS
    IF     `the sum is paid, or treated as paid, to or for the benefit of the earner`
       AND `the sum is chargeable to tax by virtue of section 225 or 226 of ITEPA 2003`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any sum paid (or treated as paid) ... which is chargeable to tax by virtue of section 225 or 226"

-- s 4(6C): the contributions limit is the amount specified by the regulations for the whole of a tax year; an equivalent
-- for earners paid weekly or at other intervals may exceed the arithmetical equivalent by not more than GBP 1.
-- src:90 | (6C) The contributions limit is the amount specified by regulations made under subsection (6A) as the contributions limit for the whole of a tax year; but—
-- src:91 | (a) the regulations may make other provision about that limit, including provision prescribing an equivalent of that limit for earners paid weekly or at other intervals; and
-- src:92 | (b) if an equivalent is prescribed, the regulations may prescribe an amount which exceeds by not more than £1 the amount which is the arithmetical equivalent of that limit.
@ref s 4(6C) (src:90-92)
GIVEN `the prescribed equivalent of the limit` IS A NUMBER
      `the arithmetical equivalent of the limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(6C)(b) the regulations may prescribe the amount as an equivalent of the contributions limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the prescribed equivalent of the limit` GREATER THAN `the arithmetical equivalent of the limit`
           AND `the prescribed equivalent of the limit` AT MOST (`the arithmetical equivalent of the limit` PLUS 1) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the prescribed equivalent of the limit` GREATER THAN (`the arithmetical equivalent of the limit` PLUS 1) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to prescribe "an amount which exceeds by not more than £1" the arithmetical equivalent; "may prescribe ... not more than" limits a grant and is no flat negative, and (b) has no "only" (the word "including" is in paragraph (a))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an amount that does not exceed the arithmetical equivalent is not addressed by paragraph (b); paragraph (a) allows an equivalent but says no more

-- s 4(6E): expressions used in subsection (6A) and in the benefits code have the same meaning in (6A) as in that code.
-- The benefits-code meaning itself is outside these sources: it is asked as a fact where needed.
DECLARE `s 4(6E) Where the meaning comes from` IS ONE OF
    `s 4(6E) the meaning the expression has in the benefits code`

-- src:97 | (6E) Expressions which are used in subsection (6A) and the benefits code have the same meaning in that subsection as they have in that code.
@ref s 4(6E) (src:97-97)
GIVEN `the expression is used both in subsection (6A) and in the benefits code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 4(6E) Where the meaning comes from`
`s 4(6E) the meaning of the expression in subsection (6A)` MEANS
    IF `the expression is used both in subsection (6A) and in the benefits code`
    THEN JUST `s 4(6E) the meaning the expression has in the benefits code`
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Expressions which are used in subsection (6A) and the benefits code"

§§ `s 4A Earnings of workers supplied by service companies etc.`

-- s 4A(1): the three conditions on which regulations may treat relevant payments or benefits as earnings paid to the worker.
-- The regulations themselves (the "IR35" rules) are outside these sources.
-- src:100 | (1) Regulations may make provision for securing that where—
-- src:101 | (a) an individual (“the worker”) personally performs, or is under an obligation personally to perform, services for the purposes of a business carried on by another person (“the client”),
-- src:102 | (b) the performance of those services by the worker is (within the meaning of the regulations) referable to arrangements involving a third person (and not referable to any contract between the client and the worker), and
-- src:103 | (c) the circumstances are such that, were the services to be performed by the worker under a contract between him and the client, he would be regarded for the purposes of the applicable provisions of this Act as employed in employed earner’s employment by the client,
-- src:104 | relevant payments or benefits are, to the specified extent, to be treated for those purposes as earnings paid to the worker in respect of an employed earner’s employment of his.
@ref s 4A(1) (src:100-104)
GIVEN `the worker personally performs, or is under an obligation personally to perform, services for the purposes of a business carried on by the client` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the performance of those services is, within the meaning of the regulations, referable to arrangements involving a third person and not referable to any contract between the client and the worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `were the services performed under a contract between the worker and the client, the worker would be regarded for the purposes of the applicable provisions of this Act as employed in employed earner's employment by the client` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1) the regulations may treat relevant payments or benefits as earnings paid to the worker in respect of an employed earner's employment` MEANS
    IF     `the worker personally performs, or is under an obligation personally to perform, services for the purposes of a business carried on by the client`
       AND `the performance of those services is, within the meaning of the regulations, referable to arrangements involving a third person and not referable to any contract between the client and the worker`
       AND `were the services performed under a contract between the worker and the client, the worker would be regarded for the purposes of the applicable provisions of this Act as employed in employed earner's employment by the client`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given "where" all three conditions hold; outside them the section is silent

-- s 4A(2)(a): "the intermediary" means (i) the third person, where that person has the specified relationship with
-- the worker, or (ii) where not, any other person with both specified relationships. "specified" relationships are
-- made by regulations outside these sources, so each is an input.
DECLARE `s 4A(2) Who is the intermediary` IS ONE OF
    `s 4A(2)(a)(i) the third person`
    `s 4A(2)(a)(ii) another person who has both relationships`
    `s 4A(2) nobody is the intermediary on these facts`

-- src:105 | (2) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:106 | (a) “the intermediary” means—
-- src:107 | (i) where the third person mentioned in subsection (1)(b) above has such a contractual or other relationship with the worker as may be specified, that third person, or
-- src:108 | (ii) where that third person does not have such a relationship with the worker, any other person who has both such a relationship with the worker and such a direct or indirect contractual or other relationship with the third person as may be specified; and
@ref s 4A(2)(a) (src:105-108)
GIVEN `the third person has such a contractual or other relationship with the worker as may be specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another person has both such a relationship with the worker and such a direct or indirect relationship with the third person as may be specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 4A(2) Who is the intermediary`
`s 4A(2)(a) who the intermediary is` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the third person has such a contractual or other relationship with the worker as may be specified` THEN `s 4A(2)(a)(i) the third person`
        IF `another person has both such a relationship with the worker and such a direct or indirect relationship with the third person as may be specified` THEN `s 4A(2)(a)(ii) another person who has both relationships`
        OTHERWISE `s 4A(2) nobody is the intermediary on these facts`    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the intermediary” means" the persons in (i) and (ii)

DECLARE `s 4A(2)(b) Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 4A(2)(b)(i) a person with whom the worker holds any office or employment`
    `s 4A(2)(b)(ii) a body corporate, unincorporated body or partnership of which the worker is a member`
    `s 4A(2)(b) a person of another kind`

-- src:109 | (b) a person may be the intermediary despite being—
-- src:110 | (i) a person with whom the worker holds any office or employment, or
-- src:111 | (ii) a body corporate, unincorporated body or partnership of which the worker is a member;
@ref s 4A(2)(b) (src:109-111)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 4A(2)(b) Kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(2)(b) the person may be the intermediary despite being a person of the kind` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 4A(2)(b)(i) a person with whom the worker holds any office or employment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4A(2)(b)(ii) a body corporate, unincorporated body or partnership of which the worker is a member` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4A(2)(b) a person of another kind` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (b) removes two possible objections and says nothing of other kinds

-- src:112 | and subsection (1) above applies whether or not the client is a person with whom the worker holds any office or employment.
@ref s 4A(2) (src:112-112)
GIVEN `the client is a person with whom the worker holds an office or employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(2) subsection (1) applies whether or not the client is a person with whom the worker holds an office or employment` MEANS
    IF `the client is a person with whom the worker holds an office or employment` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST TRUE    -- the closing words of (2): both answers are "applies"

-- s 4A(3)(a): "the worker's attributable earnings" are the specified amount of relevant payments or benefits.
-- src:113 | (3) Regulations under this section may, in particular, make provision—
-- src:114 | (a) for the worker to be treated for the purposes of the applicable provisions of this Act, in relation to the specified amount of relevant payments or benefits (the worker’s “attributable earnings”), as employed in employed earner’s employment by the intermediary;
@ref s 4A(3)(a) (src:113-114)
GIVEN `the specified amount of the relevant payments or benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4A(3)(a) the worker's attributable earnings` MEANS `the specified amount of the relevant payments or benefits`

-- s 4A(6): the four defined terms. The Parts of the Act are named by their labels in the text.
DECLARE `s 4A(6) Part of this Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 4A(6) Part I`
    `s 4A(6) Part II`
    `s 4A(6) Part III`
    `s 4A(6) Part IV`
    `s 4A(6) Part V`
    `s 4A(6) a Part after Part V`

-- src:137 | (6) In this section—
-- src:138 | “the applicable provisions of this Act” means this Part of this Act and Parts II to V below;
@ref s 4A(6) (src:137-138)
GIVEN part IS A `s 4A(6) Part of this Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(6) the Part is among the applicable provisions of this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `s 4A(6) a Part after Part V` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the applicable provisions of this Act” means this Part of this Act and Parts II to V below"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 4A(6) Kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `s 4A(6) a government department or public or local authority, in the United Kingdom or elsewhere`
    `s 4A(6) a body corporate, unincorporated body or partnership`
    `s 4A(6) a body of another kind`

-- src:139 | “business” includes any activity carried on—
-- src:140 | by a government department or public or local authority (in the United Kingdom or elsewhere), or
-- src:141 | by a body corporate, unincorporated body or partnership;
@ref s 4A(6) (src:139-141)
GIVEN carriedOnBy IS A `s 4A(6) Kind of body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(6) the activity carried on by the body is a business` MEANS
    CONSIDER carriedOnBy
    WHEN `s 4A(6) a government department or public or local authority, in the United Kingdom or elsewhere` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4A(6) a body corporate, unincorporated body or partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4A(6) a body of another kind` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“business” includes any activity carried on" by those bodies; the list is not closed

-- src:142 | “relevant payments or benefits” means payments or benefits of any specified description made or provided (whether to the intermediary or the worker or otherwise) in connection with the performance by the worker of the services in question;
@ref s 4A(6) (src:142-142)
GIVEN `the payments or benefits are of a specified description` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are made or provided in connection with the performance by the worker of the services in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(6) the payments or benefits are relevant payments or benefits` MEANS
    IF `the payments or benefits are of a specified description` AND `they are made or provided in connection with the performance by the worker of the services in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant payments or benefits” means payments or benefits of any specified description made or provided ... in connection with the performance by the worker of the services in question"

-- src:143 | “specified” means prescribed by or determined in accordance with regulations under this section.
@ref s 4A(6) (src:143-143)
GIVEN `the description is prescribed by, or determined in accordance with, regulations under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(6) the description is specified` MEANS
    IF `the description is prescribed by, or determined in accordance with, regulations under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“specified” means prescribed by or determined in accordance with regulations under this section"

-- s 4A(7): a reference to the performance of services includes the obligation to perform them mentioned in (1)(a).
-- src:144 | (7) Any reference in this section to the performance by the worker of any services includes a reference to any such obligation of his to perform them as is mentioned in subsection (1)(a) above.
@ref s 4A(7) (src:144-144)
GIVEN `the worker performs the services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the worker is under an obligation personally to perform the services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(7) the worker is treated as performing the services` MEANS
    IF `the worker performs the services` OR `the worker is under an obligation personally to perform the services`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the reference "includes" the obligation; nothing is said of a worker who does neither

§§ `s 4B Earnings: power to make retrospective provision in consequence of retrospective tax legislation`

-- s 4B(3): a "relevant power" means a power to make regulations under any of the four sections.
DECLARE `s 4B(3) Provision conferring a power to make regulations` IS ONE OF
    `s 4B(3)(a) section 3`
    `s 4B(3)(b) section 4(6)`
    `s 4B(3)(c) section 4A`
    `s 4B(3)(d) section 4AA`
    `s 4B(3) another provision`

-- src:167 | (3) A “relevant power” means a power to make regulations under any of the following provisions—
-- src:168 | (a) section 3 (power to prescribe the manner and basis of the calculation or estimation of earnings);
-- src:169 | (b) section 4(6) (power to treat amounts chargeable to income tax under the employment income Parts of ITEPA 2003 as earnings);
-- src:170 | (c) section 4A (power to treat payments or benefits to workers supplied by service companies etc as earnings).
-- src:171 | (d) section 4AA (power to make provision in relation to limited liability partnerships)
@ref s 4B(3) (src:167-171)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 4B(3) Provision conferring a power to make regulations`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4B(3) the power is a relevant power` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 4B(3) another provision` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “relevant power” means a power to make regulations under any of the following provisions"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 4B(4): it makes no difference whether the retrospective tax provision was passed or made before the day on which
-- the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed.
-- src:172 | (4) It does not matter whether the retrospective tax provision in question was passed or made before the day on which the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed.
@ref s 4B(4) (src:172-172)
GIVEN `the retrospective tax provision was passed or made before the day on which the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4B(4) the retrospective tax provision counts` MEANS
    IF `the retrospective tax provision was passed or made before the day on which the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST TRUE    -- "It does not matter whether": both answers are "counts"

-- s 4B(5): nothing in (2) authorises regulations with effect in relation to any time before 2 December 2004.
-- src:173 | (5) But nothing in subsection (2) authorises regulations to be made which have effect in relation to any time before 2nd December 2004.
@ref s 4B(5) (src:173-173)
GIVEN `the time to which the regulations would have effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4B(5) subsection (2) authorises regulations that have effect in relation to the time` MEANS
    IF `the time to which the regulations would have effect` LESS THAN (Date 2 12 2004)
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in subsection (2) authorises regulations to be made which have effect in relation to any time before 2nd December 2004"
    ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): from 2 December 2004 subsection (2) authorises only "if it appears to the Treasury to be expedient"

-- s 4B(7): the three terms defined for (8) and (9). Each is the figure or fact the regulations produce.
-- src:175 | (7) In such a case, subsections (8) and (9) apply and in those subsections and this subsection—
-- src:176 | “relevant contributions legislation” means any contributions legislation for the purposes of which the regulations have the effect mentioned in subsection (6);
-- src:177 | “the relevant time” means the time before the regulations are made mentioned in that subsection;
-- src:178 | “the revised earnings” means the earnings, in respect of the employment, paid to or for the benefit of the earner at the relevant time as determined after applying the regulations.
@ref s 4B(7) (src:175-178)
GIVEN `the earnings as determined after applying the regulations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4B(7) the revised earnings` MEANS `the earnings as determined after applying the regulations`

DECLARE `s 4B(8) Kind of reference` IS ONE OF
    `s 4B(8)(a) a reference to the earnings paid to or for the benefit of the earner at the relevant time`
    `s 4B(8)(b) a reference to the amount of such earnings so paid at that time`
    `s 4B(8) a reference of another kind`

DECLARE `s 4B(8) How the reference is read` IS ONE OF
    `s 4B(8) read as a reference to the revised earnings`
    `s 4B(8) read as a reference to the amount of the revised earnings`

-- src:179 | (8) References in any relevant contributions legislation, or any provision made under any such legislation, which relate to—
-- src:180 | (a) the earnings, in respect of the employment, paid to or for the benefit of the earner at the relevant time, or
-- src:181 | (b) the amount of such earnings so paid at that time,
-- src:182 | are to be read, in so far as they so relate, as references which relate to the revised earnings or, as the case may be, the amount of those earnings.
-- src:190 | (11) Subsections (7) to (10) are subject to any express provision to the contrary (including any such provision made by regulations under section 4C(1)).
@ref s 4B(8), s 4B(11) (src:179-182) (src:190-190)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 4B(8) Kind of reference`
      `subsections (8) and (9) apply because regulations under a relevant power made by virtue of subsection (2) affect earnings paid at a time before they are made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an express provision to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 4B(8) How the reference is read`
`s 4B(8) how the reference in the relevant contributions legislation is read` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `subsections (8) and (9) apply because regulations under a relevant power made by virtue of subsection (2) affect earnings paid at a time before they are made` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsections (8) and (9) apply "In such a case"
        IF `there is an express provision to the contrary` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (11), "subject to any express provision to the contrary"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER kind
            WHEN `s 4B(8)(a) a reference to the earnings paid to or for the benefit of the earner at the relevant time` THEN JUST `s 4B(8) read as a reference to the revised earnings`
            WHEN `s 4B(8)(b) a reference to the amount of such earnings so paid at that time` THEN JUST `s 4B(8) read as a reference to the amount of the revised earnings`
            WHEN `s 4B(8) a reference of another kind` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in so far as they so relate"

-- src:183 | (9) Any matter which, at the time when the regulations are made, has been determined for the purposes of any relevant contributions legislation, or any provision made under any such legislation, wholly or partly by reference to—
-- src:184 | (a) the earnings, in respect of the employment, paid to or for the benefit of the earner at the relevant time, or
-- src:185 | (b) the amount of such earnings so paid at that time,
-- src:186 | is to be redetermined as it would have been determined at the time of the original determination if it had been determined wholly or partly, as the case may be, by reference to the revised earnings or the amount of those earnings.
@ref s 4B(9) (src:183-186)
GIVEN `the matter was determined, before the regulations were made, wholly or partly by reference to the earnings paid at the relevant time or their amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsections (8) and (9) apply because regulations under a relevant power made by virtue of subsection (2) affect earnings paid at a time before they are made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an express provision to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4B(9) the matter is to be redetermined by reference to the revised earnings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is an express provision to the contrary` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (11), "subject to any express provision to the contrary"
        IF     `subsections (8) and (9) apply because regulations under a relevant power made by virtue of subsection (2) affect earnings paid at a time before they are made`
           AND `the matter was determined, before the regulations were made, wholly or partly by reference to the earnings paid at the relevant time or their amount` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (9) speaks of "any matter which ... has been determined" by that reference

DECLARE `s 4B(10) Kind of matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 4B(10)(a) whether Class 1 contributions are payable in respect of earnings paid in a tax week`
    `s 4B(10)(b) the amount of any such contribution`
    `s 4B(10) a matter of another kind`

-- src:187 | (10) The matters referred to in subsection (9) may include—
-- src:188 | (a) whether Class 1 contributions are payable in respect of earnings paid to or for the benefit of the earner in a tax week, and
-- src:189 | (b) the amount of any such contribution.
@ref s 4B(10) (src:187-189)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 4B(10) Kind of matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4B(10) the matter is among the matters referred to in subsection (9)` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 4B(10)(a) whether Class 1 contributions are payable in respect of earnings paid in a tax week` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4B(10)(b) the amount of any such contribution` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4B(10) a matter of another kind` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The matters referred to in subsection (9) may include"

-- src:192 | (13) For the purposes of this section “contributions legislation” means any Part of this Act or provision of such a Part.
@ref s 4B(13) (src:192-192)
GIVEN `the thing is a Part of this Act or a provision of such a Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4B(13) the thing is contributions legislation` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a Part of this Act or a provision of such a Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“contributions legislation” means any Part of this Act or provision of such a Part"

§§ `s 4C Power to make provision in consequence of provision made by or by virtue of section 4B(2) etc`

-- s 4C(4): regulations under (1) may be retrospective but must not have effect in relation to any time before 2 December 2004.
-- src:205 | (4) Regulations under subsection (1) may be made so as to have retrospective effect but must not have effect in relation to any time before 2nd December 2004.
@ref s 4C(4) (src:205-205)
GIVEN `the time to which the regulations would have effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4C(4) regulations under subsection (1) may have effect in relation to the time` MEANS
    IF `the time to which the regulations would have effect` LESS THAN (Date 2 12 2004)
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not have effect in relation to any time before 2nd December 2004"
    ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): from 2 December 2004 the text says "may be made so as to have retrospective effect" and no more; the grant is of RETROSPECTIVE effect and this function holds only the time, not the day the regulations are made, so a time inside the limit may or may not be retrospective; the flat negative speaks only of times before 2 December 2004

-- s 4C(7): the protection of entitlement. If the operative provisions would, directly or indirectly, remove a person's entitlement
-- to a contributory benefit, contribution-based jobseeker's allowance or statutory payment, or reduce its amount, they are to be
-- read with the modifications needed to prevent that effect.
-- src:218 | (7) If (ignoring this subsection) the operative provisions would directly or indirectly have effect in any case so as—
-- src:219 | (a) to remove a person's entitlement to a contributory benefit, contribution-based jobseeker's allowance or statutory payment, or
-- src:220 | (b) to reduce the amount of any such benefit, allowance or payment to which a person has an entitlement,
-- src:221 | those provisions are to be read with such modifications as are necessary to ensure that they do not have that effect.
@ref s 4C(7) (src:218-221)
GIVEN `the operative provisions would, directly or indirectly, remove a person's entitlement to a contributory benefit, contribution-based jobseeker's allowance or statutory payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the operative provisions would, directly or indirectly, reduce the amount of such a benefit, allowance or payment to which a person has an entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4C(7) the operative provisions are to be read with the modifications necessary to prevent that effect` MEANS
    IF     `the operative provisions would, directly or indirectly, remove a person's entitlement to a contributory benefit, contribution-based jobseeker's allowance or statutory payment`
        OR `the operative provisions would, directly or indirectly, reduce the amount of such a benefit, allowance or payment to which a person has an entitlement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If (ignoring this subsection) the operative provisions would directly or indirectly have effect in any case so as (a) to remove ... or (b) to reduce ..., those provisions are to be read with such modifications" (marginal reading M1(a))

DECLARE `s 4C(8) Provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 4C(8)(a) section 4B(7) to (10)`
    `s 4C(8)(a) a provision made by virtue of section 4B(2)`
    `s 4C(8)(a) a provision made under subsection (1)`
    `s 4C(8) a provision of another kind`

-- src:222 | (8) For the purposes of subsection (7)—
-- src:223 | (a) “the operative provisions” are section 4B(7) to (10) and any provision made by virtue of section 4B(2) or under subsection (1) of this section;
@ref s 4C(8)(a) (src:222-223)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 4C(8) Provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4C(8)(a) the provision is one of the operative provisions` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 4C(8)(a) section 4B(7) to (10)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4C(8)(a) a provision made by virtue of section 4B(2)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4C(8)(a) a provision made under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4C(8) a provision of another kind` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "“the operative provisions” are ..." names the provisions without "only" (marginal reading M2)

-- src:222 | (8) For the purposes of subsection (7)—
-- src:223 | (a) “the operative provisions” are section 4B(7) to (10) and any provision made by virtue of section 4B(2) or under subsection (1) of this section;
-- src:224 | (b) a person's “entitlement” includes any future entitlement which the person may have.
@ref s 4C(8)(b) (src:222-224)
GIVEN `the entitlement is a future entitlement which the person may have` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4C(8)(b) the entitlement is within the person's entitlement` MEANS
    IF `the entitlement is a future entitlement which the person may have`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a person’s “entitlement” includes any future entitlement"

-- s 4C(11): the three definitions. The day on which the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed is not in
-- these sources: it is an input.
-- src:227 | (11) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:228 | “the commencement day” means the day on which the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed;
@ref s 4C(11) (src:227-228)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day on which the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4C(11) the day is the commencement day` MEANS
    IF day EQUALS `the day on which the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the commencement day” means the day on which the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed"

-- src:227 | (11) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:228 | “the commencement day” means the day on which the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed;
-- src:229 | “enactment” includes an instrument made under an Act;
@ref s 4C(11) (src:227-229)
GIVEN `it is an instrument made under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4C(11) the thing is an enactment` MEANS
    IF `it is an instrument made under an Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“enactment” includes an instrument made under an Act"

-- src:227 | (11) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:228 | “the commencement day” means the day on which the National Insurance Contributions Act 2006 was passed;
-- src:229 | “enactment” includes an instrument made under an Act;
-- src:230 | “statutory payment” means—
-- src:231 | statutory sick pay, statutory maternity pay, statutory paternity pay, statutory adoption pay , statutory shared parental pay , statutory parental bereavement pay or statutory neonatal care pay; or
-- src:232 | any other payment prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury with the concurrence of the Secretary of State.
@ref s 4C(11) (src:227-232)
GIVEN payment IS A MAYBE `Statutory payment`
      `it is another payment prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury with the concurrence of the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4C(11) the payment is a statutory payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER payment
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `it is another payment prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury with the concurrence of the Secretary of State`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“statutory payment” means" the seven payments "or any other payment prescribed"
